 "notes": "Main result chosen: Plimpton-Lawton Coulomb-law bound (purple curve in Figs. 1 and 7), which the paper highlights as extending beyond Cavendish-like laboratory limits; the paper's other bound (AFM/Casimir, red curve, chi>~0.3 over 0.1-10 eV) is much weaker and entirely inside existing exclusions. Curve computed analytically from Eq. (26): chi = sqrt(gamma/((1-gamma)g(m)-h(m))) with h,g from Eqs. (25a,b), R*=0.61 m, R=0.76 m, sensitivity gamma=3.3e-10 (1 uV galvanometer accuracy / 3 kV). Verified against the vector Fig. 7 (purple region boundary agrees to <0.03 dex over the full plotted range). Points span the chi=1 crossings (2.74e-11 eV to 3.93e+02 eV); the bound diverges below m~0.02 neV as stated in the text. Not a dark-matter search, so no rho_DM dependence. No statistical confidence level is stated (bound from instrument sensitivity); 0.95 entered as default.",
